From 77786b71d7256e45e1fd3de592fb167385f22b76 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SRI <sri@example.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 11:26:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix onboarding persistence, editable profile, and
 post-recording workflow

- SessionViewModel now checks for a saved UserEntity on launch and
  restores myUserId/myName/myLanguage from Room instead of always
  starting fresh (setMyIdentity previously only wrote to in-memory
  StateFlow, so language + name were lost, and the app looked stuck
  re-showing the language screen on every restart).
- setMyIdentity now persists the user record (added the missing
  phoneNumber param, wired through from OnboardingScreen).
- Added updateMyProfile() plus an edit-profile dialog on HomeScreen,
  since there was previously no way to change a saved name/language.
- NavGraph's splash route now waits for that check before deciding
  whether to show language selection or skip straight to Home.
- Fixed a stale-state bug in the recording workflow: starting a
  second session reused the previous session's pairingConnected/
  myConsent/document/etc. from SessionUiState, which could skip
  pairing/consent entirely or jump straight to the prior document.
  Added resetForNewSession() called from startAsInitiator/
  joinAsScanner, and cancel the previous document-observer Job so
  an old session's Room updates can't overwrite current state.
- Fixed back-stack: Start Session is now popped when continuing to
  Consent, and DocumentScreen has an explicit Back to Home action,
  so leaving a finished record lands on Home instead of a stale
  pairing screen.
